# Simple Words Summary First

When explaining a finding, root cause, status, or plan to the user, **lead with a short summary in plain language** — before tables, IDs, commit hashes, or deep mechanics.

## Must do

- Open with 2–5 short sentences a non-expert can follow.
- Say what broke, why in everyday terms, and what we will do next.
- Put evidence, metrics, and code detail **after** that summary (or only if asked).

```text
❌ BAD: Jump straight into resource_id churn, predecessor negate, and reconcile deltas.
✅ GOOD: "GCP reused the disk name under a new id. Mongo has the cost; ClickHouse missed it. We will fold new ids onto the existing disk, then rebuild that account."
```
